{
 "_about": "A grenade's bounce as 0.69d plays it (the owner, 2026-11-16: only what 0.69d changed; docs/notes/grenade_bounce.md, \"0.69d's bounces\"). The bounce is the grenade material's (45) collision_sound in game_materials/material.pairs (grenade::on_collision 0x248980). 0.69d points 21 of its pairs at two composites of its own, weapons/f1_surface_hit (ground, default, concrete, asphalt, stone, gravel, grass, ground_forest, brick, the woods, schiefer, glass_hard, wood_bridge) and weapons/f1_metal_hit (metall_thin, metall_thick, rabitz, metal_car, metal_gas_tank, metall_tank), from the pack grenade-hits-069d; five of them (glass_hard, metal_car, metal_gas_tank, wood_bridge, metall_tank) had no bounce sound. Only collision_sound and its type change: no particle, decal or physics field. The pairs 0.69d leaves silent stay silent (mud, water, deep_water, bodies, foliage, glass, plastic, paper, cloth, rubber, the gratings, wood_tree, glass_car, foliage_dry, grass_soft, restrictor). The stock samples grenade-bounce-1 retuned are no longer played.",
